TA-cronbeat
====

Collects scheduled-job heartbeat data: all systemd timers (next elapsed, last elapsed, last-run timestamps) via systemctl list-timers, plus a count of cron jobs from /etc/crontab and /etc/cron.d. Emits JSON events to index=main (sourcetype cronbeat:status) and cronbeat.* metrics (timer totals, stale timers, cron job count) to index=metrics (sourcetype cronbeat:metrics), with dashboards.

Prerequisites
-------------
  * systemd (list-timers); cron directories read directly if present
  * Splunk Enterprise or Universal Forwarder 9.x - 10.6 (forwarder recommended
    on monitored hosts).
  * A metrics-typed index (default name: metrics) on the indexer:

      [metrics]
      datatype = metric

    Forwarders only need that index to exist on the indexer side.
  * No network egress, no root requirement beyond the Splunk service account.
    Fully standalone add-on with no dependencies.

Install
-------
Install on each monitored host (Apps > Install app from file, splunk install
app, or deployment server), restart Splunk, then verify:

  index=main sourcetype="cronbeat:status" | head

Search quick reference
----------------------
  index=main sourcetype="cronbeat:status" | head
  | mcatalog values(metric_name) where index=metrics metric_name="cronbeat.*" by host
  | mstats avg("cronbeat.*") where index=metrics span=60s by host

Usage
-----
Events: index=main sourcetype=cronbeat:status  (per-timer next/last elapsed; cron job count; stale flag)
Metrics: cronbeat.timers_total, cronbeat.timers_stale, cronbeat.cron_jobs on index=metrics
A timer whose 'last' is >24h old is flagged stale (alarm).
Dashboards: TA-Cronbeat > Cronbeat Overview / Cronbeat Metrics

Configure
---------
Override the interval or destination index in etc/apps/TA-cronbeat/local/inputs.conf
(never edit default/).

Troubleshooting
---------------
  * Stale = timer has a last-run but it is more than 24h old; never-run timers are not stale.
  * cron_jobs counts lines matching a time field, skipping comments.

License
-------
SOURCE-AVAILABLE (see LICENSE) - free personal, educational and evaluation
use; commercial or production use requires a paid license from BentleyPC
LLC (https://www.bentleypc.com/TA-cronbeat).

Enter your key (format BP-...) after purchase using EITHER method:

  1. Splunk Web: open the app, click "License" in the nav, click a row to
     open the key entry page, paste the key and Save.

  2. File (headless / forwarder friendly): create the file
     $SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/TA-cronbeat/local/license.conf with:

         [settings]
         telemetry_enabled = 1
         key = BP-xxxxxxxxxxxx

     No restart required - the hourly beacon reads this file on every run.

Set telemetry_enabled = 0 to keep the key for validation but pause all
outbound beacons. The beacon sends only: license key, hostname, app name
and app version to the BentleyPC license API (see api_base in
default/license.conf). It is telemetry only - never a license check that
blocks functionality.
